# Agent Braid licensing

Copyright © 2026 Juan Antonio Yáñez García.

Agent Braid uses a split-license model so that its executable artifacts remain
open under strong network copyleft while its research and documentation remain
freely reusable with attribution and share-alike obligations.

## Software — AGPL-3.0-only

The following material is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 only (`AGPL-3.0-only`):

- `.github/workflows/**`
- `agent_braid/**`
- `examples/**`
- `schemas/**`
- `scripts/**`
- future source code, build definitions, executable fixtures, and automation,
  unless a file explicitly states another license

The complete license text is in
[`LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt`](LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt).

## Documentation and research — CC-BY-SA-4.0

The following material is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International license (`CC-BY-SA-4.0`):

- the root Markdown documentation, including the Constitution, architecture,
  research program, mathematical foundations, roadmap, governance,
  contribution guide, security policy, and terminology
- `docs/**`
- `reports/**`
- `research/**`
- `CITATION.cff`, `.github/CODEOWNERS`, and `.gitignore`

The complete license text is in
[`LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt).

## Legal and third-party material

This file, `NOTICE`, and `TRADEMARKS.md` may be reproduced as necessary to
identify the applicable terms and comply with them. The canonical license texts
in `LICENSES/` remain subject to their own notices. Third-party material, if
introduced, retains its stated license and must be documented explicitly.

## Attribution and marks

Spec Kit 1.0.7 third-party scaffolding under `.specify/scripts/**`, unmodified
base templates, and adapter-generated metadata retains MIT terms; see
`LICENSES/Spec-Kit-MIT.txt` and `docs/development/THIRD_PARTY.md`.
Vendored and repository-adapted Python skill files under
`.agents/skills/{api-design,cli-development,code-quality,documentation,testing-strategy}/**`
and the matching `.claude/skills/` paths retain MIT terms; see
`LICENSES/python-skills-MIT.txt` and `.agents/skills/VENDORED-SKILLS.md`.
Our `.specify/templates/overrides/**`, Spec Kit editorial skill bodies and `specs/**`
documentation use `CC-BY-SA-4.0`. Own generators, validators, tests and executable
pilot material use `AGPL-3.0-only`. Generated files retain the terms of their
source portions; adapter metadata does not imply GitHub authored our policies.

Redistributions and adaptations must preserve the attribution and notices
required by the applicable license and clearly identify modifications. No
copyright license in this repository grants permission to use Agent Braid names,
logos, or other source-identifying marks except for truthful referential use.
See [`TRADEMARKS.md`](TRADEMARKS.md).

If a path could reasonably fall into more than one category, the license stated
in that file controls. If the file contains no license statement, documentation
uses `CC-BY-SA-4.0` and software or executable material uses `AGPL-3.0-only`.
